flapus is distributed under the three-clause BSD license (text below).

The FLAC encoder and decoder were written for flapus from the FLAC specification
(RFC 9639); they contain no code from libFLAC. The apodization window shapes and the
coefficient quantization follow libFLAC's documented behaviour (BSD, Copyright
Xiph.Org Foundation and Josh Coalson). FLAC is free of patents.

The Opus part is a reimplementation of the Opus reference software. Its algorithms,
tables and numeric behaviour are derived from the following BSD-licensed projects:

libopus 1.6.1 (codec: CELT, SILK, analysis, multistream, repacketizer)
  Copyright 2001-2023 Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Octasic,
                      Jean-Marc Valin, Timothy B. Terriberry,
                      CSIRO, Gregory Maxwell, Mark Borgerding,
                      Erik de Castro Lopo, Mozilla, Amazon

opus-tools 0.2 (opusenc/opusdec behaviour: WAV input, downmix, dither, WAV output)
  Copyright (c) 2002-2007 Jean-Marc Valin
  Copyright (c) 2008 CSIRO
  Copyright (c) 2007-2018 Xiph.Org Foundation
  Copyright 2000-2002, Michael Smith; 2010, Monty

libopusenc 0.3 (encoder buffering, LPC extension, Ogg packing)
  Copyright (c) 1994-2013 Xiph.Org Foundation and contributors
  Copyright (c) 2017 Jean-Marc Valin

opusfile 0.12 (decoder link handling, pre-skip/end trimming, stereo downmix)
  Copyright (c) 1994-2013 Xiph.Org Foundation and contributors

Speex resampler (used by opusenc and opusdec)
  Copyright (C) 2007-2008 Jean-Marc Valin
  Copyright (C) 2008 Thorvald Natvig

